{"ts": "2026-10-17T09:23:10.815528Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T0922Z-5dcd", "unit": "openspec:add-recurrent-tree-indexing", "seq": 13, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-001", "target": "C-b54f84ac", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "satisfied as it stands. test_is_online_only_detects_placeholder (packages/core/tests/test_tree_index.py) proves placeholder detection; the default text pass no longer reads an online-only file (task 2.2 guard, proven by the new test_index_tree_text_content_skips_online_only_file: the extract_markdown spy never sees cloud.txt and its manifest row stays metadata); binary content is read only with --content (want_binary needs the content flag), so a default run records every placeholder from stat only.", "text_sha256": "bff22b340a4c032c0dd61f7a32c5ea16ccfcd2be22b4e1bd3c5230d087f6c984", "answer_sha256": "23efc6ef73b1e3a407749587c8f1166be8edbf634572dd7a2a02db9d6f79c884"}
{"ts": "2026-10-17T09:23:10.816465Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T0922Z-5dcd", "unit": "openspec:add-recurrent-tree-indexing", "seq": 14, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-002", "target": "C-1ccce576", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "satisfied as it stands. test_render_file_record_includes_type_location_and_siblings asserts the name, the type label, the size, the folder location, the sibling names and the mtime date; test_render_file_record_flags_online_only asserts the online-only flag; test_index_tree_metadata_only_indexes_every_file shows photo.jpg recorded by index-tree as a metadata memory.", "text_sha256": "451d979cbbe237eed3c333a1903fbd96886166bf1ccfa1ba59279fddc7b9a3da", "answer_sha256": "03df638fcc52c1f367c0448ee986f5adcaaeac5fe2cdd97f56c1470db108aa63"}
{"ts": "2026-10-17T09:23:10.817100Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T0922Z-5dcd", "unit": "openspec:add-recurrent-tree-indexing", "seq": 15, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "C-99b1ee27", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "satisfied as it stands. test_index_tree_is_idempotent shows a second run over an unchanged tree adds no memory; test_index_tree_reindexes_changed_file shows the changed a.md has exactly one active record and the old one archived (replaced, not duplicated); index_tree calls store.manifest_upsert for each re-indexed file, and the new test_index_tree_content_run_upgrades_metadata_row_without_force checks the manifest row after a re-index.", "text_sha256": "89a28b5871c711054c5f64a7a04195d16fcfbb1b5e857516a134169d817dcc4e", "answer_sha256": "794cfb2f11f85b153af481478a22e6b2b80a7de686d56eb3cbbeb2e9a6f67d28"}
{"ts": "2026-10-17T09:23:10.817663Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T0922Z-5dcd", "unit": "openspec:add-recurrent-tree-indexing", "seq": 16, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-4a833fcd", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "satisfied as it stands. index_tree stops binary and content reads once the --max-download-mb budget is spent (budget_hit), the remaining files fall back to metadata-only, and the report prints the row budget: reached - remaining files metadata-only. The new test_index_tree_budget_exhausted_online_only_text_counted runs --content --content-types txt --max-download-mb 0.000001 and asserts exactly one file read, one content and one metadata manifest row, and the budget row printed.", "text_sha256": "a85b6a41a2448cd798b4a9de89ad1cce947b78b5e03688fb4b8d7c2c73a0177c", "answer_sha256": "ce3e2005d86f2e9b95fd1463c6d1a7e06137607882e6f33193bc2146a2bb3ebc"}
